title: 'frame-omni-bencher: force the linker not to drop jemalloc shim on Linux'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: "Force the linker to keep the polkadot_jemalloc_shim crate and its\
    \ #[global_allocator]. Without it, the linker might drop it since it is seen as\
    \ a dependency with no referenced symbols. The issue happens only on a subset\
    \ of combination of rust version and linker (e.g. on CI with Ubunti 24.04, rust\
    \ 1.88.0 + gcc/ld strips the jemalloc crate from the binary but not rust 1.92.0\
    \ and also rust 1.88.0 + clang/mold works fine\r\n"
crates:
- name: frame-omni-bencher
  bump: patch
